  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased Collaboration</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of influencing activities held with policymakers, companies, influential decision-makers on key STITCH Lobby and Advocacy goals/strategies</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Influencing activities include dialogues, meetings, consultations, briefings, seminars, workshops, conferences, summits, etc. held with policymakers, companies, influential decision-makers on main STITCH issues, claims and policy goals</narrative>
    </description>
    <reference code="SCS092" indicator-uri="https://helpdesk-opendata-minbuza.nl/indicator-codelist/" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline iso-date="2021-01-01" value="0" year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Baseline: According to ITUC&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s Global Rights Index (ITUC, 2021), the situation for trade unions and freedom of association in India is worsened from 2020 to 2021, being classified as a country with No guarantee of rights.Target: STITCH aims to conduct 98 L&amp;A activities with different actors such as government officials, political leaders, media personnel, directly engaged brands (member brands of ETI or FW), indirectly engaged brands (not member brands of ETI or FW), TUs/ LRO and other actors towards improvement of labor rights.Achieved: In 2021, the focus of L&amp;A activities was on Influencing labour codes and it&apos;s rules with timely recommendation and lobbying for gender sensitive policies</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="1">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">There was one planned activity around a study on Access to Remedy</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="31">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Due to definitional changes we classified all the influencing work done to help develop and launch the new MSS (Tirupur Stakeholder Forum) here. In previous years meetings held 1:1 with influential actors that helped to form this were not counted. Future targets will reflect the increase in</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="10"></target>
     <actual value="19">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mostly to do with developing multi stakeholder dialogues in Tirupur.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2025-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="10">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Various, mostly to do with supporting the TSF</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="19">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Various, mostly to do with supporting the TSF</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="3">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">ETI in India aims to conduct 3 L&amp;A activities with different actors such as government officials, political leaders, media personnel, directly engaged brands (member brands of ETI or FW), indirectly engaged brands (not member brands of ETI or FW), TUs/ LRO and other actors towards improvement of labor rights.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="1"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of functional coalitions/networks/platforms in which STITCH participates</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coalitions are partnerships among distinct actors that coordinate action in pursuit of shared goals. Networks are forms of organization characterized by voluntary and reciprocal patterns of communication and exchange. Platform is a declaration of the principles on which a group of persons stands. This is a joint activity indicator (with contributions from multiple STITCH partners), and is only reported by this STITCH partner to avoid double counting</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline iso-date="2021-01-01" value="0" year="2021"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="4"></target>
     <actual value="0">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">ETI India team had been exploring opportunities to collaborate with existing networks and platforms. Scoping exercise to find relevant networks and platforms is underway. Within the Indian garment industry, there are few successful networks and platforms opertional. In May 2022, ETI India team met representatives from various multi-stakeholder platforms that were active in Tamil Nadu a few years ago but found out that they either cease to exist today or are not functional. ETI India also showed support to the joint work being done by ARISA and Cividep by encouraging brands&apos; country teams to participate in the former&apos;s work in Bangalore. Few exploratory conversations have also taken place with a national level labour rights network who have a special focus on migrant workers. As these efforts are still in its  nascent stage, we have not reported the same above.However, as of 2022 we decided instead to work on the development of our own MSS/Multi-stakeholder platforms and not joining other coalitions in India.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="1"></target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
